Improve the parsing of SEL RTAC project exports (``peat parse -d selrtac``). PEAT now parses the XML that recent versions of ACSELERATOR RTAC export, including Structured Text POUs (``<Content>``), GOOSE messages, C37.118 PMU channels, tag lists, system time settings, user libraries, global variable lists, data types, shared ``POUs`` objects, "Advanced Read-in Items", and ``Project Info.xml``. PEAT now gets the RTAC model and part number from the export (``Project Info.xml`` and the ``DeviceMOT`` of each file) instead of always using "3530", and adds the Ethernet interfaces, host name, remote IP addresses, ports, protocols, protocol registers, and the Structured Text logic (``logic.st``) to the device data. PEAT can also find RTAC XML files by their ``<RTACModule>`` root element. Six public, openly licensed RTAC project exports were added as test data, with their sources and licenses in ``tests/modules/sel/data_files/rtac/SOURCES.md``. The new "RTACs" section of the SEL documentation describes the export format.
